       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. At this dose, the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nHere are a few things you might have meant:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg.\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me the clinical reason and I can enter it with a note, though I'd recommend pharmacist review first."
      }
