       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Confirming it doesn't change the safety problem. 5,100 mg/day is exactly double the maximum labeled daily dose of metformin, and I can't think of a clinical situation that justifies it. You also haven't given a rationale. In a patient with normal renal function, this dose carries a real risk of severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** I can do that right away, for example 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or 1,000 mg PO twice daily.\n- **Check for a transcription error.** The intended dose may have been 1,700 mg/day total, or 850 mg per dose.\n- **Consult pharmacy or the attending.** If you think this off-label dose is warranted, a pharmacist or attending can review it and place the order directly through the proper override process.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
